  "id": "COMPOUND:18445 - PROTEIN:5003",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Etiocholandiol may interact with ME-180 through multiple pathways, with some of the targets being shared across different relationships. The first pathway links Etiocholandiol to COUP transcription factor 2, which is then targeted by Capryl caprate, and finally by ME-180. The second and third pathways connect Etiocholandiol to Fucosyltransferase 6, which is targeted by two different compounds—(1R)-1-(7,8-dimethoxy-2,2-dimethylchromen-6-yl)ethanol and p-alpha-Dimethyl styrene—both of which also target ME-180. These findings indicate that Etiocholandiol may influence ME-180 through distinct but related molecular mechanisms, possibly involving transcriptional regulation and enzyme activity. The evidence is consistent with a role for Etiocholandiol in modulating ME-180 through multiple biological processes, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
